INFO:agent.loop:\u26a1 Executing tool: 'knowledge_agent' with arguments: {"source_title": "OneCoin DOJ compensation announcement and sentencing summary", "source_url": "https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/justice-department-announces-compensation-process-onecoin-fraud-victims-funds-recovered; https://www.afslaw.com/perspectives/investigations-blog/co-founder-fraudulent-cryptocurrency-sentenced-20-years-prison", "text": "SRC-001 (DOJ, April 13 2026): Between 2014 and 2019, Ruja Ignatova and Karl Sebastian Greenwood, identified as co-founders of OneCoin Ltd., and others orchestrated an international cryptocurrency investment scheme. OneCoin began operations in 2014, was based in Sofia, Bulgaria, and marketed/sold a fraudulent cryptocurrency through a global multi-level-marketing network. Misrepresentations led victims to invest over $4 billion worldwide. DOJ says several key figures were sentenced and criminal forfeiture was pursued; more than $40 million in forfeited assets was available for victim compensation. FBI/IRS-CI investigated; DOJ continues pursuing Ignatova, described as an FBI Top Ten Fugitive. SRC-002 (ArentFox Schiff, Sept. 15 2023): Greenwood, a Swedish and UK citizen and OneCoin co-founder, was sentenced to 20 years for his alleged role in a $4 billion fraud scheme and ordered to forfeit about $300,000. The article reports prosecutors alleged OneCoin claims that its value was determined by supply/demand though it was arbitrarily set; that Greenwood claimed a private blockchain existed though no publicly verifiable blockchain existed; and that a global MLM network paid commissions for recruitment. It reports Greenwood was OneCoin’s top MLM distributor and allegedly earned 5% of monthly sales, over $300 million. The article says Ruja Ignatova, the other co-founder, remained at large and was added to the FBI Top Ten Most Wanted List in June 2022. These source texts do not establish Ignatova's current whereabouts, death, or whether she is alive."}
